Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.02,0:00:25.58,Main,Lorraine,0,0,0,,Rentt's heading back into \Nthe labyrinth today...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.03,0:00:33.37,Main,Lorraine,0,0,0,,No, he's not supposed to go until \Nthe kidnapping thing calms down.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.41,0:00:37.56,Main,Lorraine,0,0,0,,It wouldn't kill him to take the day off...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.58,0:00:42.06,Main,Lorraine,0,0,0,,Nah, I suppose that's impossible for him.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.24,0:02:20.69,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,Not bad.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.69,0:02:23.59,Main,Clope,0,0,0,,I've made some adjustments just for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.59,0:02:26.70,Main,Clope,0,0,0,,Since I know your habits.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.21,0:02:29.59,Italics,Rentt,0,0,0,,{\an8}He definitely knows who I am...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.25,0:02:31.58,Title,Sign,0,0,0,,{\an1\shad0\bord2\fs17\fade(1000,400)\c&H908A88&\3c&H000000&\b1\pos(493.343,275.946)}A New Weapon\Nand Power
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.14,0:02:34.76,Main,Clope,0,0,0,,{\an8}I've given it the ability to use mana, \Nspirit energy, and divinity, just like you asked.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:34.76,0:02:36.61,Main,Clope,0,0,0,,Try it out.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.61,0:02:37.71,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,Okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.97,0:02:39.70,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,First, magic.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.84,0:02:50.11,Main,Clope,0,0,0,,Wow... you're a lot stronger now.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.53,0:02:53.18,Main,Clope,0,0,0,,Your mana seems way more powerful.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.18,0:02:56.70,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,All I can do is try and force \Nit into the sword, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:57.13,0:02:59.75,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,But I do have some degree of \Ncontrol over my spirit energy.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.18,0:03:11.99,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,And lastly, divinity.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.49,0:03:20.87,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,This is a good sword.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.87,0:03:23.17,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,Infusing it with divinity \Ndidn't harm it at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:23.17,0:03:26.63,Main,Clope,0,0,0,,Look... it's sprouted new leaves.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:27.40,0:03:29.23,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,An effect of the divinity?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:30.13,0:03:33.27,Main,Clope,0,0,0,,It's the only thing I can think of...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.27,0:03:37.13,Main,Clope,0,0,0,,Hey, how are you able to use divinity?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.13,0:03:39.89,Main,Clope,0,0,0,,That's normally given to \Nyou by the gods, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.29,0:03:44.36,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,I once repaired a shrine \Nthat had been abandoned.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.36,0:03:46.83,Main,Clope,0,0,0,,You're more of a believer than I thought.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.83,0:03:48.60,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,I just felt like doing it \Nfor some reason, is all.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.60,0:03:50.89,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,I don't even know what god it was.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.62,0:03:55.52,Italics,Rentt,0,0,0,,It must've been a lower-ranking \None, I'm sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.06,0:03:59.56,Main,Clope,0,0,0,,Hey, can I keep this?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.56,0:04:02.34,Main,Clope,0,0,0,,If these sprouts grow, they \Nmight have divinity in them.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.34,0:04:04.00,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,Fine with me.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.00,0:04:05.06,Main,Clope,0,0,0,,Thanks.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.89,0:04:08.05,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,Can I practice a little more?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.31,0:04:10.51,Main,Clope,0,0,0,,Sure. What are you going to do, though?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.51,0:04:12.24,Main,Clope,0,0,0,,You've tried everything, haven't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.91,0:04:16.29,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,I want to try them all at once.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:19.19,0:04:20.57,Main,Clope,0,0,0,,Will this do?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.97,0:04:21.86,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.95,0:04:25.86,Main,Clope,0,0,0,,Have you ever heard of Mana-Spirit Fusion?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.86,0:04:28.23,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,I've heard rumors.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.23,0:04:30.81,Main,Clope,0,0,0,,It's a technique that allows you \Nto massively power up your magic
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.81,0:04:33.81,Main,Clope,0,0,0,,and spirit skills by using \Nthem both at the same time.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.81,0:04:35.86,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,You'd have to be a real master to do that.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.86,0:04:37.36,Main,Clope,0,0,0,,Of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.36,0:04:40.71,Main,Clope,0,0,0,,You screw it up, and your \Nbody explodes, I've heard.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.80,0:04:43.43,Main,Clope,0,0,0,,Want to back out?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.43,0:04:45.21,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,No, I'll try it.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.93,0:04:49.89,Italics,Rentt,0,0,0,,An explosion wouldn't be enough \Nto kill this body, anyway.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.89,0:04:50.51,Main,Clope,0,0,0,,Here.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.47,0:04:52.96,Main,Clope,0,0,0,,Use this.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.96,0:04:55.68,Main,Clope,0,0,0,,If this breaks in the process, it's no loss.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.95,0:04:57.11,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,You're sure?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.11,0:05:03.62,Main,Clope,0,0,0,,Yeah. It can't handle divinity, but \Nit's a lot cheaper than a new sword.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.62,0:05:05.28,Main,Clope,0,0,0,,Perfect for testing.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.42,0:05:11.77,Italics,Rentt,0,0,0,,Okay. First, I put my mana into my sword \Nand spirit energy into my hand...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.65,0:05:15.04,Main,Clope,0,0,0,,I-Is that...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.09,0:05:18.37,Italics,Rentt,0,0,0,,This is tough...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.37,0:05:22.46,Italics,Rentt,0,0,0,,It's like I'm trying to jam something \Ninto a box that's already full.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.92,0:05:26.35,Italics,Rentt,0,0,0,,This is bad... I can't keep it up...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.72,0:05:36.39,Main,Clope,0,0,0,,Hey... are you going to add \Ndivinity to what you just did?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.39,0:05:37.88,Main,Clope,0,0,0,,That's really dangerous!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.62,0:05:39.68,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,I am.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.72,0:05:48.95,Italics,Rentt,0,0,0,,I need power...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.95,0:05:52.07,Italics,Rentt,0,0,0,,If I'm going to be a \NMythril-class adventurer!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.91,0:06:00.12,Main,Clope,0,0,0,,Y-You okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.12,0:06:01.36,Main,Clope,0,0,0,,That looks like trouble!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.05,0:06:09.61,Main,Clope,0,0,0,,Hey, the sword can't take any more of that!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.31,0:06:27.99,Main,Clope,0,0,0,,The sword turned into a ball?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.29,0:06:30.45,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,I'm sorry... your sword...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.45,0:06:31.79,Main,Clope,0,0,0,,It's fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.79,0:06:37.67,Main,Clope,0,0,0,,Divinity has the power to remove impurity \Nand restore matter to its original state.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.19,0:06:40.90,Main,Clope,0,0,0,,So you can't use it with a normal weapon,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.90,0:06:43.12,Main,Clope,0,0,0,,'cause it'll break the bonds \Nholding the it together.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.84,0:06:49.56,Main,Clope,0,0,0,,This sword's made to handle divinity, \Nbut it can't take what you just did.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.56,0:06:52.65,Main,Clope,0,0,0,,The most you could do is Mana-Spirit Fusion.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.88,0:07:04.77,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,Hey... what do I do if I find an \Nenemy I can't defeat with that?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.77,0:07:08.31,Main,Clope,0,0,0,,You want me to make you a dozen that \Nyou just carry around with you?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.07,0:07:11.15,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,I don't have the money.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.15,0:07:12.76,Main,Clope,0,0,0,,I know that.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.75,0:07:22.94,Italics,Rentt,0,0,0,,I'm gonna need good equipment if \NI'm going to become a Mythril.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.94,0:07:25.17,Italics,Rentt,0,0,0,,I need to make a lot of money.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.17,0:07:26.54,Main,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,Please!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.54,0:07:28.36,Main,Adventurer,0,0,0,,It's not happening!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.74,0:07:29.79,Main,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.79,0:07:32.64,Main,Adventurer,0,0,0,,I can't take a job that \Ndoesn't come from the guild!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.64,0:07:34.00,Main,Adventurer,0,0,0,,It'll cause a huge \Nmess for me later.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.00,0:07:36.86,Main,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,Please! I'm begging you!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.86,0:07:38.48,Main,Adventurer,0,0,0,,You need to learn when to shut up.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.48,0:07:40.50,Main,Adventurer,0,0,0,,Or do I need to teach you?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.50,0:07:41.11,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,Hey.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.05,0:07:46.18,Main,Adventurer,0,0,0,,Wh-Who are you? You look weird...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.45,0:07:48.13,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,Let me talk to him.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.80,0:07:52.88,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,I think I can take him for all he's worth.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.57,0:07:57.00,Main,Adventurer,0,0,0,,Do what you want with him.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.27,0:07:58.87,Main,Adventurer,0,0,0,,Bye, kid.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.87,0:08:02.51,Main,Adventurer,0,0,0,,He says he'll talk to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.51,0:08:03.87,Main,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,Um...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.87,0:08:04.64,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,Hey.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.33,0:08:07.66,Main,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,Who are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.66,0:08:09.00,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,An adventurer.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.82,0:08:13.81,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,I can't promise I'll take the job, \Nbut I can at least hear you out.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:13.81,0:08:15.12,Main,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,Really?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.12,0:08:15.91,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.33,0:08:21.67,Main,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,Please defeat the Lord... \Nthe Lord of the Lake!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.09,0:08:24.66,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,The "Lord of the Lake"?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.14,0:08:35.34,Italics,Rentt,0,0,0,,What a mess this is...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.34,0:08:38.21,Italics,Rentt,0,0,0,,The reward, and the quest itself, \Nare both full of problems.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.99,0:08:42.98,Flashback,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,My name is Ryuntus. I'm from Tottsu village.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:42.98,0:08:47.68,Flashback,Rentt,0,0,0,,Right. The one that's several \Ndays to the east, correct?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.68,0:08:49.37,Flashback,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,You know it?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.37,0:08:51.73,Flashback,Rentt,0,0,0,,I've heard they have a strange festival.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.73,0:08:52.54,Flashback,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.99,0:08:56.77,Flashback,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,There's a legend that they once offered \Nup a young, beautiful girl whose body
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.77,0:09:00.40,Flashback,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,was brimming with mana to the Lord of the \NLake, in exchange for saving the village.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.26,0:09:06.35,Flashback,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,They still hold a festival once \Na year to remember that day.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.61,0:09:10.15,Flashback,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,But this time the Lord of the \NLake actually appeared,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.15,0:09:12.60,Flashback,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,and ate the girl who was playing \Nthe role of the sacrifice!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:16.05,0:09:17.11,Flashback,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,And...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.11,0:09:20.05,Flashback,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,It's started demanding more sacrifices.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.05,0:09:22.61,Flashback,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,Several of the village \Ngirls have already died...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.61,0:09:24.18,Flashback,Rentt,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.18,0:09:25.65,Flashback,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,Help us!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.65,0:09:29.32,Flashback,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,The next sacrifice is my little sister!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.73,0:09:32.24,Flashback,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,Please!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.13,0:09:39.80,Italics,Rentt,0,0,0,,Ryuntus's wish is to save his \Nsister, not to kill a monster.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.54,0:09:44.33,Italics,Rentt,0,0,0,,There's no need to fight \Nthe Lord of the Lake.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.48,0:09:47.13,Italics,Rentt,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.13,0:09:49.51,Italics,Rentt,0,0,0,,Something feels really wrong about this.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.28,0:09:53.99,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,It's a quiet village.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:53.99,0:09:58.96,Main,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,Yes. It's a small village, but \Nit used to be much more lively.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:58.96,0:10:04.06,Main,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,But since the Lord of the Lake appeared, \Neverybody's just gotten so tired...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.19,0:10:10.13,Main,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,This way, Rentt.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.13,0:10:11.06,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.99,0:10:15.32,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,What's this mark?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.32,0:10:16.85,Main,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,It's a sign.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.85,0:10:22.21,Main,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,The house with this mark has to be the next to \Noffer their daughter up to the Lord of the Lake.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.21,0:10:24.54,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,Did the Lord of the Lake put it there?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.54,0:10:29.84,Main,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,No, it lives deep in the \Nlake. No one's ever seen it.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:29.84,0:10:34.09,Main,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,It was probably put here \Nby a Kelpie that serves it.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.09,0:10:37.95,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,A {\i1}Kelpie{\i0}? That's a powerful monster.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.95,0:10:39.69,Main,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,It is?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.69,0:10:40.85,Main,Amiris,0,0,0,,Brother?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.39,0:10:43.71,Main,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,Amiris! I'm back!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:43.71,0:10:45.71,Main,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,This is Rentt, the adventurer!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.71,0:10:47.91,Main,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,He's a Bronze-class!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.20,0:10:49.67,Main,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,He's going to save you!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.67,0:10:50.69,Main,Amiris,0,0,0,,Jeez!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.94,0:10:56.36,Main,Amiris,0,0,0,,Brother, I told you so many times not to \Ntalk to any weirdos when you went to the city!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.36,0:10:58.72,Main,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,But Rentt's a good guy!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:58.72,0:11:01.48,Main,Amiris,0,0,0,,You only think that because \Nhe's tricking you!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.16,0:11:05.39,Main,Amiris,0,0,0,,He looks like a weirdo to me!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:05.64,0:11:07.19,Italics,Rentt,0,0,0,,That's really mean...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:07.19,0:11:11.49,Italics,Rentt,0,0,0,,I can hear every word since my senses \Ngot better when I became a monster...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.35,0:11:15.43,Main,Amiris,0,0,0,,You're Rentt, the adventurer, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.43,0:11:16.55,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.55,0:11:21.23,Main,Amiris,0,0,0,,Thank you for listening \Nto my foolish brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.23,0:11:23.06,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,No, it's fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.64,0:11:29.58,Main,Amiris,0,0,0,,But the festival of Tottsu village \Nis an ancient tradition.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.58,0:11:32.29,Main,Amiris,0,0,0,,I can't selfishly ask to be \Nthe one girl excused from it.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.29,0:11:33.63,Main,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,Amiris!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:33.63,0:11:37.77,Main,Amiris,0,0,0,,Please, forget what he asked you, and leave.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.69,0:11:41.46,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,I was hired by Ryuntus.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:42.20,0:11:45.61,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,Only Ryuntus has the right \Nto rescind the request.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.85,0:11:50.48,Main,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,I'm not rescinding it! Ever!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.27,0:11:57.74,Main,Amiris,0,0,0,,If you're going to be staying in \Nthis village, please use our home.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:57.74,0:12:01.24,Main,Amiris,0,0,0,,But please don't interfere \Nwith the festival.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:01.86,0:12:05.54,Main,Amiris,0,0,0,,I'm glad to become the sacrifice.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.78,0:12:10.16,Main,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,I'm sorry my sister's so stubborn.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.46,0:12:12.78,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,The festival's tomorrow night?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.78,0:12:13.94,Main,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:13.94,0:12:18.44,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,From the look of it, Amiris is not \Ngoing to run if we tell her to.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.27,0:12:21.55,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,What will you do?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.35,0:12:24.96,Main,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,I know it's very dangerous.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.96,0:12:29.80,Main,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,But if there's any chance my sister \Ncan be saved... I'll do anything!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.80,0:12:32.39,Main,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,So please!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.64,0:12:40.21,Main,Villagers,0,0,0,,Hey, mister, what are you selling?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:40.21,0:12:42.32,Main,Merchant,0,0,0,,This is dried meat.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.29,0:12:44.78,Main,Villagers,0,0,0,,And this?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.78,0:12:49.06,Main,Merchant,0,0,0,,Dried fruits. Here, try some.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:49.06,0:12:50.38,Main,Villagers,0,0,0,,Really?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.38,0:12:51.99,Main,Villagers,0,0,0,,It looks so good!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:51.99,0:12:55.83,Main,Merchant,0,0,0,,But I do have a request...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.83,0:12:56.99,Main,Villagers,0,0,0,,What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.99,0:13:01.28,Main,Merchant,0,0,0,,Tell your parents to buy something.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.28,0:13:04.76,Main,Merchant,0,0,0,,I can't sell anything \Nbecause nobody's coming!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:04.76,0:13:05.61,Main,Villagers,0,0,0,,Okay!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.61,0:13:06.83,Main,Villagers,0,0,0,,I'll tell them!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.83,0:13:08.29,Main,Merchant,0,0,0,,Great. Eat up.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.29,0:13:09.90,Main,Villagers,0,0,0,,Thank you!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.89,0:13:14.52,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,I'm sorry... I want to ask you something.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.76,0:13:16.98,Main,Villagers,0,0,0,,A monster!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.98,0:13:17.68,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,A mons-
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.68,0:13:18.81,Main,Villagers,0,0,0,,He'll eat us!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:18.81,0:13:21.55,Main,Merchant,0,0,0,,I've never seen you in this village before.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.55,0:13:23.48,Main,Merchant,0,0,0,,Here for the festival?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.48,0:13:25.45,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,Something like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.45,0:13:27.77,Main,Merchant,0,0,0,,You came at a bad time, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.77,0:13:31.58,Main,Merchant,0,0,0,,The Lord of the Lake is angry right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:32.74,0:13:37.25,Main,Merchant,0,0,0,,And so the villagers have better things \Nto do than buy my wares, I guess!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.25,0:13:38.45,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.45,0:13:39.82,Main,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,Rentt!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.82,0:13:41.59,Main,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,Lunch is ready!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:41.95,0:13:43.09,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,Okay!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.09,0:13:45.62,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,Sorry to interrupt your business.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.62,0:13:47.54,Main,Merchant,0,0,0,,It's fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:47.54,0:13:50.99,Main,Merchant,0,0,0,,You should give up on the \Nfestival and head back to town.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.99,0:13:52.00,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,All right.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:52.38,0:13:54.78,Main,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,Did you get to take a look at the lake?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.78,0:13:55.72,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.72,0:13:58.86,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,Anyway... does that merchant come often?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:58.86,0:14:04.05,Main,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,Yes. They stop here often. \NIt's quite nice of them.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:04.61,0:14:06.16,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.74,0:14:18.71,Main,Woman,0,0,0,,Forgive us, Amiris.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:18.71,0:14:21.51,Main,Amiris,0,0,0,,No, don't apologize.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:21.51,0:14:23.92,Main,Amiris,0,0,0,,The Lord was the one who chose me.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.45,0:14:29.64,Main,Woman,0,0,0,,I was sure Ryuntus would \Ntake you and run away...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.38,0:14:36.97,Main,Woman,0,0,0,,He was telling everybody we \Nshould call off the festival...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:36.97,0:14:38.34,Main,Amiris,0,0,0,,He was?!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.69,0:14:44.27,Main,Amiris,0,0,0,,If we make the Lord angry, it could \Neasily destroy this village!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.27,0:14:51.77,Main,Woman,0,0,0,,He was so desperate... he was worried about \Nyou, but also the future of this village.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.18,0:14:57.13,Main,Amiris,0,0,0,,He really is such a fool...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.18,0:15:11.76,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,Amiris, can we talk?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.76,0:15:14.10,Main,Amiris,0,0,0,,No! Don't come in!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.10,0:15:16.89,Main,Amiris,0,0,0,,The sacrifice must not\N meet others so casually!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.32,0:15:19.88,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,All right. Then I'll say it here.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.79,0:15:22.47,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,I'll take care of things.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:23.65,0:15:26.94,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,There's always a way.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.94,0:15:28.22,Main,Amiris,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:28.22,0:15:29.82,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,I'm serious.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.82,0:15:31.65,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,So you must struggle, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.18,0:15:35.90,Main,Amiris,0,0,0,,Struggle? How?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:35.90,0:15:38.37,Main,Amiris,0,0,0,,No human could defeat the Lord of the Lake!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:38.88,0:15:42.28,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,Ryuntus and I will handle \Nthe Lord of the Lake.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.28,0:15:45.00,Main,Amiris,0,0,0,,That's impossible!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.00,0:15:48.87,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,Amiris, don't do anything \Nto make your brother sad.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.28,0:15:51.49,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,He's all the family you have, isn't he?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.93,0:15:54.35,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,So struggle.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.70,0:15:56.63,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,As long as there's hope...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.18,0:15:59.38,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,That's all I wanted to say.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.62,0:16:06.82,Main,Amiris,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.39,0:16:12.96,Main,Man,0,0,0,,Our Lord, who protects us from \Nthe bottom of the lake...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:12.96,0:16:20.14,Main,Man,0,0,0,,Each time the horns of your servants \Nleave their mark, we make our sacrifice.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.14,0:16:24.45,Main,Man,0,0,0,,One sacrifice of treasure, \None, of our daughters.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.45,0:16:27.85,Main,Man,0,0,0,,When the azure light guides,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.85,0:16:32.39,Main,Man,0,0,0,,protect us from disaster...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.25,0:16:34.80,Main,Man,0,0,0,,I'm sorry, Amiris.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:34.80,0:16:36.61,Main,Man,0,0,0,,We must do this to protect the villlage.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.61,0:16:38.75,Main,Amiris,0,0,0,,I know, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.75,0:16:41.72,Main,Man,0,0,0,,Do your duty well.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:47.89,0:16:49.11,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,Let's go.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:49.11,0:16:49.84,Main,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.52,0:16:52.69,Main,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,Amiris, are you ready?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.24,0:16:55.93,Main,Amiris,0,0,0,,Yes. Let's go.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:08.75,0:17:10.55,Main,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,Rentt! The fog!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:10.55,0:17:13.80,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,Yeah. It appeared at just the right time.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:13.80,0:17:16.36,Main,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,I can't see a thing...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.36,0:17:17.97,Main,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,Let's turn back!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:19.03,0:17:20.27,Main,Amiris,0,0,0,,The orb...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.27,0:17:23.39,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,Looks like our "Lord" has \Nmade his appearance.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:24.52,0:17:26.35,Main,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,Rentt, there's something there!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:31.30,0:17:33.73,Main,Amiris,0,0,0,,This is the Lord of the Lake?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.68,0:17:37.77,Main,Amiris,0,0,0,,Lord, please, calm your anger!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.77,0:17:40.96,Main,Amiris,0,0,0,,Protect the village! Protect the village!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.46,0:17:40.96,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,Stop, Amiris.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.96,0:17:41.99,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,You're wasting your time.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.99,0:17:45.16,Main,Amiris,0,0,0,,I'll sacrifice myself... I'll \Nsacrifice myself, so...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.11,0:17:47.21,Main,Amiris,0,0,0,,The orb!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.43,0:17:49.37,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,It's just a beacon, nothing more.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:50.12,0:17:51.21,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,Hang on to the ship!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.99,0:17:55.87,Main,Amiris,0,0,0,,He's floating on the water?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.87,0:17:59.49,Italics,Rentt,0,0,0,,It's nice to have a friend \Nwho's an alchemist.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.36,0:18:06.72,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,Now, then... let's show this \N"Lord" for what he really is.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.43,0:18:12.14,Italics,Rentt,0,0,0,,Krakens are normally found in the ocean.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.14,0:18:13.67,Italics,Rentt,0,0,0,,They don't spit fire, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.73,0:18:16.88,Italics,Rentt,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.51,0:18:21.02,Main,Merchants,0,0,0,,It's that weirdo from this afternoon!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:21.02,0:18:22.38,Italics,Rentt,0,0,0,,Just like I thought.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.29,0:18:28.36,Italics,Rentt,0,0,0,,A mage cast an illusion on the fog, \Nand then fired Fortia Bolivus.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:29.66,0:18:34.83,Main,Merchants,0,0,0,,If you'd just left, you wouldn't \Nhave lost your precious life.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.83,0:18:39.12,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,To think the Lord of the Lake was \Njust an ugly traveling merchant.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.90,0:18:42.55,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,I've already lost my life once, anyway.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.55,0:18:45.09,Main,Merchant,0,0,0,,What the hell are you talking about?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:57.71,0:18:59.28,Main,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,Rentt!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.75,0:19:02.15,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,I'm fine. It's over.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:02.69,0:19:04.86,Main,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,What's that ship?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:05.64,0:19:07.33,Main,Amiris,0,0,0,,What is happening?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:11.88,0:19:15.75,Main,Man,0,0,0,,Amiris? Is that true?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.75,0:19:16.26,Main,Amiris,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.53,0:19:20.64,Main,Amiris,0,0,0,,They pretended to be the Lord, \Nand demanded sacrifices!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.64,0:19:22.74,Main,Man,0,0,0,,How awful...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.74,0:19:25.81,Main,Amiris,0,0,0,,Rentt, did you realize from the start?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.81,0:19:28.15,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,I did think it was suspicious.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.15,0:19:32.62,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,A monster that's been worshipped as the Lord \Nof an area doesn't just go out of control.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.62,0:19:35.88,Main,Man,0,0,0,,Hey! Where are the other girls?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:38.18,0:19:39.32,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,Answer them!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.32,0:19:40.96,Main,Merchant,0,0,0,,They're alive!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.96,0:19:43.77,Main,Merchant,0,0,0,,We were going to sell them for \Na fortune in another land!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:43.77,0:19:46.19,Main,Man,0,0,0,,They're all alive, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:46.19,0:19:48.84,Main,Merchant,0,0,0,,There's a small hut on the \Nother side of the lake.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:48.84,0:19:50.09,Main,Merchant,0,0,0,,That's where they are!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:50.79,0:19:52.12,Main,Man,0,0,0,,Get a carriage ready!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:52.12,0:19:53.58,Main,Man,0,0,0,,We need to go save them!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:53.58,0:19:54.42,Main,Man,0,0,0,,Right!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:55.30,0:19:58.78,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,Ryuntus, this means the \Njob is complete, correct?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.78,0:20:00.48,Main,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,Yes, of course!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:04.29,0:20:08.07,Main,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,We're doing the festival \Nover. Stay and watch it.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.07,0:20:11.02,Main,Amiris,0,0,0,,He's right. You don't \Nhave to leave so soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:11.02,0:20:14.52,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,Sorry. Someone's waiting for me in Maalt.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:15.51,0:20:17.42,Main,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,Too bad, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.17,0:20:23.10,Main,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,Rentt, I won't forget how you \Nsaved the village, and Amiris.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:23.10,0:20:24.70,Main,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:24.70,0:20:26.75,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,You're welcome. Be well.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:26.75,0:20:28.58,Main,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,Yes, take care!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.58,0:20:30.01,Main,Amiris,0,0,0,,Rentt!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.50,0:20:38.80,Main,Ryuntus,0,0,0,,Amiris, what did you...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:38.80,0:20:40.88,Main,Amiris,0,0,0,,I just wanted to thank him, is all!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.08,0:20:43.01,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,Thank me, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.49,0:20:45.96,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,Then I shall gladly accept your thanks.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.77,0:20:56.55,Italics,Rentt,0,0,0,,Those kidnappers said they didn't \Ngrab anyone but women...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.30,0:21:00.81,Italics,Rentt,0,0,0,,They seem to have nothing to do with \Nthe kidnappings of new adventurers
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.81,0:21:02.67,Italics,Rentt,0,0,0,,that Sheila talked about...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:04.45,0:21:08.30,Main,Lorraine,0,0,0,,I see. So Ryuntus's sister was saved, then?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:08.30,0:21:09.24,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:09.24,0:21:11.73,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,And the other girls are all safe, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:11.73,0:21:13.26,Main,Lorraine,0,0,0,,Excellent.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:13.63,0:21:15.87,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,It's thanks to the magic item you lent me.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:16.25,0:21:19.14,Main,Lorraine,0,0,0,,It's nice to be able to \Nwalk on water, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:19.14,0:21:20.29,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:20.68,0:21:25.66,Main,Lorraine,0,0,0,,If it was real, I would've loved \Nto see the Lord of the Lake.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:25.66,0:21:27.57,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,You were right not to go.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:27.57,0:21:29.62,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,You had a rush job, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:30.80,0:21:32.72,Main,Lorraine,0,0,0,,By the way, Rentt.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.46,0:21:38.93,Main,Lorraine,0,0,0,,You stole the heart of another \Ngirl you saved, didn't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:39.38,0:21:41.42,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,Of course not.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:41.42,0:21:44.06,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,I did get a thank you, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:44.06,0:21:45.57,Main,Lorraine,0,0,0,,A thank you, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:47.15,0:21:49.34,Main,Lorraine,0,0,0,,I'm sure she'll...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:49.34,0:21:52.72,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,She'll forget me before much \Ntime has passed at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:54.60,0:21:56.86,Main,Rentt,0,0,0,,That's how it is when you're an adventurer.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:59.88,0:22:02.89,Main,Lorraine,0,0,0,,The gods should punish \Nyou a little, I think.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:35.72,0:23:40.01,Title,Preview,0,0,0,,{\shad0\bord2\fs33\c&H2B2C54&\3c&HC5E4F6&\b0\pos(194.175,272.715)}Dragonblood Flower
